  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening and Promoting Consular Support For Stranded Migrants in Libya</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to strengthen and promote consular support services for stranded migrants in Libya, to facilitate their safe, voluntary, and dignified return to their countries of origin. This support will also build a foundation to provide migrants in Libya with legal identity. The project outcomes are for migrants stranded in Libya to access faster and more effective consular services. IOM will collaborate closely with embassies in Libya on establishing an online consular service that facilitates communication and coordination between migrants and their embassy representatives. The project will also ensure authorities of target migrant origin countries are aware of existing key bottlenecks that prevent effective consular support, and ways to address issues, and the embassy staff of target migrants&#x2019; origin countries have the skills and tools to provide efficient consular service support to nationals. Lastly the project will support embassies of migrant countries of origin to have political dialogue on legal and policy developments and lessons sharing on legal and policy recommendations, and ways to strengthen consular coordination and service support systems.</narrative>
  </description>
